\begin_layout Enumerate
Sourcing the setup script
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=bash"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

source /opt/ros/foxy/setup.bash 
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Source your project (optional).
 When you source the main ROS install (with source /opt/ros/foxy/setup.bash)
 that makes all the installed packages available but not ones you’ve built
 yourself.
 For those you need to source your local workspace (sometimes called an
 overlay) with source install/setup.bash (called from within the workspace)
 to make its packages available.
 It can get a bit confusing but once you are used to it it’s actually a
 very practical approach for working on multiple projects.
 The following command works in the project folder:
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=bash"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

source install/setup.bash
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
A very good option to not source it every time, its to add it to the bashrc
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=bash"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

gedit ~/.bashrc
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection*
Install Colcon
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Next we need to install the build tool, colcon (I'm not sure why this isn't
 included as part of the core ROS installation).
 All we need to do is run:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=bash"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

sudo apt install python3-colcon-common-extensions
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

